# Grav core boundaries

This plugin runs on **Grav 2.x**. Treat upstream core as read-only.

## Never modify core Grav files

Do **not** edit, delete, or add files under:

| Path | What it is |
|------|------------|
| `system/` | Grav core (PHP, blueprints, default assets) |
| `vendor/` | Composer dependencies (including Grav packages) |

Also avoid hand-editing root bootstrap files unless the user explicitly asks: `index.php`, `composer.json`, `composer.lock`, and core CLI scripts under `bin/` (e.g. `bin/grav`, `bin/gpm`).

If a fix seems to require a core change, stop and use a **user-layer** approach instead (plugin hooks, blueprint overrides, or theme integration).

## Plugin patterns

- **Behavior** → `intention-header-footer-code.php`, `classes/`, API controllers, injectors
- **Admin Next UI** → `admin-next/pages/`, `admin-next/widgets/`
- **Admin forms / plugin settings** → `blueprints.yaml`
- **Presentation (admin)** → `assets/admin/`

When upgrading Grav via GPM, core and `vendor/` are replaced; this plugin directory is what you own.
